{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Which EU grid registers list this inverter, battery or wallbox? — {{ SITE }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}One table across seven national grid-connection lists (AT, BE, CZ, EE, NL, PL, SE): {{ devices|n }} inverters, hybrids, batteries, plug-in units and wallboxes, with each list's own status, firmware and dates, and a log of what changed.{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Which EU grid registers list it?</h1>
<p>Grid operators in several EU countries publish lists of the inverters, batteries and chargers they accept for connection.
None of the lists refers to the others. This table puts {{ devices|n }} models from seven of them side by side —
{{ multi|n }} appear in two or more — with each list's own status word, firmware and dates, and a
<a href="changes/">change log</a> of what was added, dropped or changed between refreshes.</p>
<p class="note"><strong>The register is the authority; this is a cross-reference.</strong> An empty cell means we found no matching
entry — the model may be listed under another name, or the list may not cover it. It never means “not approved”.
Check the list itself before you install, and ask your grid operator when in doubt.</p>

<form class="filters" id="xf" onsubmit="return false" hidden>
  <input type="search" id="q" placeholder="Search model or brand" aria-label="Search model or brand">
  <select id="brand" aria-label="Brand"><option value="">All brands</option></select>
  <select id="cls" aria-label="Device class"><option value="">All device classes</option>
    {% for k, v in RC.items() if k != 'other' %}<option value="{{ k }}">{{ v }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
  <select id="c" aria-label="Country"><option value="">Any country</option>
    {% for c in COUNTRIES %}<option value="{{ c }}">Listed in {{ c }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
  <select id="st" aria-label="Status"><option value="">Any status</option>
    <option value="R">Listed with restrictions</option><option value="T">Time-limited</option>
    <option value="P">Time-limited, date passed</option><option value="E">Expired</option><option value="N">“Nein” (AT)</option></select>
  <select id="n" aria-label="Number of registers"><option value="">In any number of lists</option>
    <option value="2">In 2 or more lists</option><option value="3">In 3 or more</option><option value="4">In 4 or more</option></select>
</form>
<p class="count" id="xcount" aria-live="polite"></p>
<div id="xv" class="xv-wrap"></div>
<p><button type="button" id="more" class="more" hidden>Show more</button></p>
<p class="legend muted">✓ listed · ✓* listed with restrictions · ⏱ time-limited · ⏱! time-limited, date passed · exp expired ·
Nein = the Austrian list's own “Nein” · empty = no matching entry found (not a “no”).</p>
<noscript><p>The table needs JavaScript. Every model is also on its brand page below.</p></noscript>

<h2>The lists</h2>
<div class="rows">
{% for c in COUNTRIES %}
{% set regs = RREG.keys()|select('in', [c, c ~ '-EV'])|list %}
<article class="row"><h3><a href="country/{{ c|lower }}/">{{ c }} — {{ RREG[c].country }}</a></h3>
<dl>
  <dt>List</dt><dd>{% for r in regs %}<a href="{{ RREG[r].url }}">{{ RREG[r].name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
  <dt>List dated</dt><dd>{% for r in regs %}{{ meta[r].source_date if r in meta else '—' }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
  <dt>Models here</dt><dd>{{ counts[c]|n }}</dd>
  <dt>We show</dt><dd>{{ RREG[c].use }}</dd>
</dl></article>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<h3>Not read (yet)</h3>
<ul class="prose small">
{% for cc, country, name, link, why in not_read %}<li><strong>{{ cc }}</strong> {{ country }} — <a href="{{ link }}">{{ name }}</a>: {{ why }}.</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p class="muted">Fourteen of thirty European countries publish no list at all: the grid operator checks an EN 50549-1 (or national) certificate per application.</p>

<h2>Latest changes</h2>
{% set e = log[0] %}
<p>{{ e.date }}: {% if e.baseline %}{{ e.note }}{% else %}{% for r, x in e.registers.items() %}{{ r }} +{{ x.added|length }} / −{{ x.removed|length }} / {{ x.changed|length }} changed{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% else %}no changes{% endfor %}{% endif %}
— <a href="changes/">all changes</a>.</p>

<h2>Brands</h2>
<p class="brand-list">{% for b, name, n in brand_links %}<a href="brand/{{ b }}/">{{ name }}</a> <span class="muted">{{ n }}</span>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
<script src="{{ rel }}static/registers.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
